        "title": "fix(store): order hydration observations durably",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- order canonical thread and revision observations by lossless RFC3339Nano source time plus a durable pre-fetch sequence\n- reject delayed hydration payloads before they can overwrite canonical threads or dependent comments, PR details, documents, and evidence\n- apply the same schema-aware freshness contract to summaries, embeddings, clustering, archive coverage, and workflow runs while preserving read-only legacy archive support\n- converge supported schema-4/6/8/9/10 stores to one canonical schema with read-only diagnostics and a stable healthy-v10 fast path\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go test ./...`\n- `go test -race ./internal/store ./internal/syncer -count=1`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go run golang.org/x/tools/cmd/deadcode@v0.45.0 -test ./...`\n- focused delayed-parent and overlapping-hydration tests repeated 20 times\n- `make generate-sqlc` followed by a clean diff\n- `go mod tidy` followed by a clean diff\n- Gitcrawl Store portable/hydration test suite against the branch binary\n\n## Exact-head real migration proof\n\nValidated at `c7c48bc0dfe6d3fc31bad73c2268ffbcfd0a2fec`:\n\n- built the released `v0.7.1` source at `10725cf8aa5daba9f8714a6774b2f7ddcaabc1e6` and created a fresh real schema-4 SQLite archive with repository, PR, revision, file, and workflow-run rows\n- opened that archive through the PR-head write path: `pragma user_version` advanced to `10`, `pragma integrity_check` returned `ok`, diagnostics reported `current`, and every seeded row survived\n- compared the complete normalized `sqlite_schema` of the migrated archive with a fresh schema-10 archive; both produced the exact SHA-256 `cec371706a14d1a446b7d31c7f1d0f8d7bb32f67e9665b4a5f91836dba87f441`\n- verified two healthy schema-10 read opens left the database byte-for-byte unchanged and created only a zero-byte WAL sidecar\n- injected supported-schema drift by deleting the allocator at persisted sequence `19`; read-only doctor reported the pending convergence without changing the database, then a write reopen rebuilt the allocator floor at `19` with integrity `ok`\n- reran delayed-parent/completion and overlapping-sync adversarial store/syncer tests `20` times successfully",
